<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Apply</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Press this button to apply any changes (new colours picked or another scheme selected) to the scene. This will affect to all windows.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Save as</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Press this button to save current colour settings as a <a class="glossterm" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1">Colour Scheme</a> <span class="glosstext" style="display:'none';" id="POPUP171588544">A defined set of colours.</span>. A dialog will appear enter scheme name in the field. Press OK to store the scheme in materials.clr file.</p>
<p class="Note" id="p1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: KUBE does not check for identical scheme names. That means if you already have a colour scheme with the same name, the new scheme will be overwrite the old one.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Delete</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Press this button to delete the currently selected colour scheme. This will remove the scheme from materials.clr file.</p>
<p class="Note" id="p2"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> Current colour settings (or chosen scheme) are used next time you run KUBE . If you set own colours for particular entities, these colours take precedence and are used in the scene.</p>
